# S7.1 (PLAN.md, acceptance scenarios): did tiling pay off? — the naive
# side. A trip of k1's main loop adds 8 f32 FLOPs and 16 global bytes
# loaded per thread, one of its remainder 2 and 4 B: 0.5 flop/B,
# shape-independent (no --bind). Contrast with S7.2 (k5, 1024 per 32 B):
# two independent runs, two comparable numbers, no diff verb. The same
# contrast shows in shared memory: the naive kernel declares none, the
# tiled one 2048 B per CTA (as `ptxas -v` reports, `bytes smem`).
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/k1/k1.sm_80.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry _Z11hgemm_naiveiiifPK6__halfS1_fPS_( // per thread: flops f32 <= (2·(param_2 mod 4) + 8·((param_2 - param_2 mod 4) / 4) + 3); global load <= (4·(param_2 mod 4) + 16·((param_2 - param_2 mod 4) / 4) + 2) B, store <= 2 B; param load 44 B{{$}}
